        <div class="blog-post-body">

          <h2>Introduction: Why Online Etiquette Matters</h2>

          <p>
            In a world where video chat and digital conversations have become part of our daily
            routine, knowing how to communicate respectfully is more important than ever. The
            internet connects us across cultures, time zones, and backgrounds — but without good
            etiquette, these conversations can easily go wrong.
          </p>

          <p>
            Platforms like <strong><a href="/">Wakiee</a></strong> have made it easier than ever
            to <a href="https://wakiee.live">talk to strangers</a> online and make international
            friends. Yet, as simple as clicking “Connect” might be, maintaining a good impression
            takes awareness and kindness. Online etiquette — often called “netiquette” — is what
            keeps these interactions meaningful and safe.
          </p>

          <h2>Online Friendship and Communication: What the Data Shows</h2>

          <p>
            Online communication is not simply a way to pass time. For many people, digital spaces
            have become places where friendships begin and continue.
          </p>

